Runtime text editor retained cumulative phase guard validation
Date: 2026-07-04 +08:00
Slice: runtime_text_editor_retained_cumulative_phase_guard_rustfmt_static_visual_cargo_deferred

Problem addressed:
- User screenshot showed DengXian editor labels where individual characters appeared shifted left/right.
- Previous guard covered shaped glyph positions, but runtime advance projection could still accept many individually small <= 0.0625px differences.
- Those small differences can accumulate across labels like editor base.zui and folder-open.svg and cross the retained host 1/8px raster placement bin.

Implementation:
- zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/layout.rs adds runtime_advances_preserve_retained_raster_bins.
- Runtime advance projection now falls back to host natural glyph placement when projected glyph origins do not share the same RetainedGlyphPlacement bin as host glyph origins.
- zircon_editor/src/ui/retained_host/host_contract/paint_text/draw/layout/tests.rs adds runtime_positioned_glyphs_rejects_cumulative_subpixel_phase_drift.

